# tmp/ is a symlink into RAM — /tmp for executables, /dev/shm for artifacts.
# Nothing under it is the record, and the link itself is machine-local, so it is
# recreated by the run scripts rather than tracked.
tmp

# output/ holds what the last program to run returned to you -- the goodbye of
# whichever tool finished most recently. It is a mailbox, not a record: the
# contents are overwritten every run and mean nothing to anyone who was not
# there. The directory is kept; the messages are not.
output/*
!output/.gitkeep

# docs/HTML/ is the documentation site, and it is built rather than written.
# Two hundred files that rewrite wholesale whenever any document changes, all of
# them derived from files already in this repository -- so tracking them would
# put the same words in the record twice and make every documentation edit look
# like two hundred. The tool is the artifact; run it and the site is there.
#
#   luajit src/149-the-documentation-site.lua
docs/HTML/
